      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely rational to feel finished when the entire narrative of your life was intertwined with his presence. Feeling like an \"error\" is a symptom of bone-deep exhaustion, not a true reflection of your worth. You don't have to \"start over,\" because rebuilding doesn't mean erasing; it means finding tiny, new ways to inhabit the life you already built. Please consider that your worth isn't tied to his care, but to your inherent right to exist simply because you are here. If the weight of continuing feels too heavy, please reach out to a crisis line immediately; they are there for moments exactly like this.",
